    <h2>Cancellation</h2>
    <p>For telehealth appointments, cancel at least 24 hours ahead or you may be charged an $85
    fee for the session.</p>
    <p>In-person walk therapy must be paid in advance to hold the spot, and there are no refunds
    for cancellations inside 48 hours.</p>

    <h2>Where you have to be</h2>
    <p>A Texas license covers clients located in Texas, so both you and your therapist must be
    physically in the state during a telehealth session. Tell your therapist in advance if you
    will be traveling and the appointment can be moved rather than canceled.</p>

    <h2>Waitlist and new clients</h2>
    <p>Clients who want to be added to the waitlist schedule a consult first. The practice's
    associates are accepting new clients, including at sliding-scale fees.</p>
    <p>Trail walk and equine work requires a consult plus one to three online sessions
    beforehand, and is for adults only.</p>
